## What agents can't do

- Read or edit `.env` files. In Claude Code, `.claude/settings.json` denies Read and Edit on `.env`, `.env.local`, `.env.*.local`, `.env.development`, `.env.dev`, `.env.production`, `.env.prod`, `.env.staging`, `.env.test`, `.env.bak` and `.env.backup`, both relative to the session folder (`**/`) and anywhere on disk (`//**/`), so a worktree session also can't read the main checkout's files.
  - Per the Claude Code permissions docs, the deny also covers Grep and Glob (best effort) and the shell file commands Claude Code recognizes (`cat`, `head`, `tail`, `sed`, redirections).
  - Sub-agents inherit it.
  - Name env files only with those suffixes.
  - The example file stays readable and editable.
- Not covered: a program that opens the file itself. Never write or run a command whose purpose is to print a `.env` value.
- Paste a secret into a PR, issue, commit, log or chat. If it happens, rotate the secret (E7).
